KoboldCpp runs AI models on your own computer. This guide takes you from download to your first chat in four steps. You don't need to know anything about AI.

{% steps %}

1. [**Download KoboldCpp**](/download/): one file from GitHub. There is no installer.

2. [**Start KoboldCpp**](/getting-started/start/): open the file. A settings window, the launcher, appears.

3. [**Choose a model and launch**](/getting-started/model/): the model is the AI itself. The launcher can download one for you.

4. [**Chat**](/getting-started/chat/): KoboldAI Lite opens in your web browser.

{% /steps %}

## What you need

- A computer with Windows, Linux, or a Mac with an Apple Silicon (M-series) chip.
- Up to about 8 GB of free disk space for KoboldCpp and a beginner model.
- A graphics card is not required. With one, replies come much faster.

Stuck at any point? See [Help and next steps](/getting-started/help/). Everything beyond the basics is in the [wiki](/docs/).
